1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,547
Business Case 04 begins when an employee or assigned agency proposes a
candidate for a job.

2
00:00:07,547 --> 00:00:13,208
A permission-bound source relationship converts into a separate
application only after validation.

3
00:00:13,208 --> 00:00:15,567
The governed record is SUB-DEMO-001.

4
00:00:15,567 --> 00:00:21,227
The accountable actors are Employee Referrer, Agency User, Candidate,
Recruiter, Partner Administrator.

5
00:00:21,227 --> 00:00:28,303
This demonstration uses synthetic browser-memory data and creates no
database, provider, message or external-system effect.

6
00:00:28,303 --> 00:00:32,901
The action-level data-flow diagram defines 4 processes before product
navigation.

7
00:00:32,901 --> 00:00:41,176
Every process identifies the actor, screen, action, input, output,
business object, event, governed store, rule, denial and recovery.

8
00:00:41,176 --> 00:00:45,774
The highlighted path keeps each business grain and version distinct.

9
00:00:45,774 --> 00:00:49,261
Process 1, Partner: Capture authority and assignment.

10
00:00:49,261 --> 00:00:55,237
The action prepare submission produces submission in validation in the
Partner ledger.

11
00:00:55,237 --> 00:00:58,724
Process 2, Recruiter: Validate duplicate and ownership.

12
00:00:58,724 --> 00:01:06,195
The action run privacy-safe validation produces accepted, returned or
disputed relationship in the Ownership ledger.

13
00:01:06,195 --> 00:01:09,183
Process 3, Recruiter: Convert to application.

14
00:01:09,183 --> 00:01:16,654
The action create controlled application produces separate application
with source lineage in the Application ledger.

15
00:01:16,654 --> 00:01:21,137
Process 4, Partner Administrator: Track fee or reward milestone.

16
00:01:21,137 --> 00:01:29,106
The action review eligibility and dispute produces approved, pending or
disputed reward in the Reward ledger.

17
00:01:29,106 --> 00:01:31,340
The actual product route is /hr/agency-assignments/AGA-DEMO-001.

18
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:36,927
It presents referral and agency validation and conversion in the
surrounding recruitment or onboarding workspace.

19
00:01:36,927 --> 00:01:46,238
The screen remains a wireframe, but its identifiers, current state,
navigation, data relationships and action boundaries match the business
contract used by the connected workbench.

20
00:01:46,238 --> 00:01:49,157
The seeded workbench follows record SUB-DEMO-001.

21
00:01:49,157 --> 00:02:06,187
Its governed fields are Assignment, AGA-DEMO-001 , Active; Job scope,
JOB-DEMO-001; Candidate permission, Recorded , expires Sep 12; Ownership
window, 90 days; Duplicate result, Possible match , owner hidden; Fee
policy, 18% on eligible start.

22
00:02:06,187 --> 00:02:15,432
Field classifications remain visible so the presenter can distinguish
public, internal, confidential and restricted projections for the active
persona.

23
00:02:15,432 --> 00:02:19,589
With Recruiter selected, we perform validate and convert submission.

24
00:02:19,589 --> 00:02:24,670
The guard requires assignment, candidate authority, duplicate and
ownership windows pass.

25
00:02:24,670 --> 00:02:35,294
The state changes from In validation to Application created, records
PartnerSubmissionConverted, writes to the Partner ledger, and creates
the handoff: Recruiter receives APP-PARTNER-001.

26
00:02:35,294 --> 00:02:39,479
We now exercise the controlled exception: Simulate ownership dispute.

27
00:02:39,479 --> 00:02:44,595
The prepared failure is Existing ownership claim is privacy-protected
and disputed.

28
00:02:44,595 --> 00:02:54,361
Unsupported downstream work stops, successful prior evidence remains
intact, and the state-change receipt assigns explicit recovery without
hiding the failed attempt.

29
00:02:54,361 --> 00:02:57,689
The owned recovery is Resolve scope and convert.

30
00:02:57,689 --> 00:03:01,848
It reuses the governed business context without duplicating completed
effects.

31
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:07,256
The new receipt preserves previous state, current state, actor, event
and correlation key.

32
00:03:07,256 --> 00:03:16,408
The control center and handoff inbox then expose the same recovery
through partner conversion, returns and dispute age and minimum-context
next-actor work.

33
00:03:16,408 --> 00:03:18,599
Business Case 04 is complete.

34
00:03:18,599 --> 00:03:31,308
We demonstrated the level-two process contract, the actual product
route, governed field projections, the primary state transition, a
controlled exception, targeted recovery, causal dashboard evidence and
the next-actor handoff.

35
00:03:31,308 --> 00:03:36,567
A permission-bound source relationship converts into a separate
application only after validation.

36
00:03:36,567 --> 00:03:41,388
Production identity, persistence, integrations and external delivery
remain separate implementation gates.
